# Private payloads consumed through requireFile: register them with
# `nix-store --add-fixed sha256 <file>` instead of tracking them here.  Local
# copies live in this directory - they are the durable copy, because no GC
# root holds the store paths.  Six are required:
#   liuqin-firmware-vpu.tar.zst and liuqin-firmware-cs35l41.tar.zst
#   (hashes in pkgs/firmware.nix), liuqin-ssc-config.tar.zst (hash in
#   examples/demo/configuration.nix, or point
#   hardware.liuqin.sensors.sscConfig at the file), the two stock DT
#   archives imported by pkgs/bootimg/stock-*.nix, and the downstream v0.3.1
#   release image (data/release-v0.3.1/boot.img, matched by *.img below)
#   whose ramdisk carries the bulk firmware tree.
# The other liuqin-firmware-* archives were replaced by the firmware tree in
# the downstream release's boot.img (pkgs/firmware.nix), so local copies of
# them are stale.
# Store copies of these payloads are not rooted and may be garbage-collected;
# the local files above are the durable copy (back them up - they are device
# dumps that cannot be regenerated). Re-register after a GC with
# `nix-store --add-fixed sha256 <basename>` (same store path, no rebuild), or
# keep an explicit GC root:
#   nix-store --add-root ~/.local/share/liuqin-payloads/<basename> \
#     --indirect -r "$(nix-store --add-fixed sha256 <basename>)"
# Beware `git clean -xdf`: everything listed below is untracked.
data/liuqin-*.tar.zst
pkgs/bootimg/stock-base-dtbs.tar.zst
pkgs/bootimg/stock-dtbo-entries.tar.zst
